source: crates/hydronode-cli/tests/c3_help.rs
expression: text
---
Queue a command. The device gets it with its next delivery and confirms or
declines it. Without --type the type is guessed from the value.

Usage: hn command [OPTIONS] <SENSOR> <NAME> <VALUE>

Arguments:
  <SENSOR>  Sensor id
  <NAME>    Command name the device listens to (for example relay1)
  <VALUE>   Value to send

Options:
      --type <TYPE>  Value type, guessed when left out [possible values: bool, int32, uint32, int64, uint64, string]
  -h, --help         Print help

Global options:
  -p, --profile <NAME>  Profile to use (server and login), see 'hn profile list'
      --json            Print JSON instead of tables (stable shape, for scripts)

Examples:
  hn command <sensor-id> relay1 true
  hn command <sensor-id> relay1 1400 --type uint32
  hn command <sensor-id> mode eco --type string
